# Aidbox live mode (bead odontogram-cpx) — generated by:
#   npm run live:provision -- --instance <reetfurt-uat-instance>
# Copying this file by hand is still allowed; never paste a real secret here.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. NEVER commit a filled-in copy.
#
# THE CREDENTIALS BELONG TO A SCOPED MACHINE CLIENT, NOT TO AN ADMIN.
# The `odontogram-live` client authenticates with HTTP Basic and is limited by
# the Aidbox AccessPolicy `odontogram-live-dental` to exactly:
#   /fhir/Patient                                    GET only
#   /fhir/Observation, /fhir/Condition,
#   /fhir/ServiceRequest, /fhir/CarePlan             GET, PUT, POST, DELETE
# and nothing else. The patient record is READ-ONLY on purpose: the odontogram
# charts teeth, it does not own the patient. DELETE is needed because clearing
# a finding has to remove its resource, or the finding would come back on the
# next load. An admin account (or any client with a wider scope) must
# never be configured here: this app runs in a browser, so whatever is put in
# these variables is compiled into the served bundle and is readable by anyone
# who can open the page. That is acceptable for a scoped development client
# against a local Aidbox, and is exactly why it must not be more than that.
#
# See docs/aidbox-live-mode.md for the Reetfurt uat:local + live:provision
# workflow and for what live mode can and cannot carry.

# Filled by live:provision from the named Reetfurt instance binding.
# The FHIR endpoint `/fhir` is appended by the app. Do not point this at the
# shared isynet Aidbox on :8081.
VITE_AIDBOX_BASE_URL=

# The scoped machine client's id and secret (Basic auth).
VITE_AIDBOX_CLIENT_ID=odontogram-live
VITE_AIDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The patient charted when the URL names none. `?patient=<id>` always wins.
VITE_DEFAULT_PATIENT_ID=
